    "text": "Two tangent galvanometers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo></math>and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> have coils of radii <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> respectively and resistance <math><mn>8</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math> each. They are connected in parallel with a cell of emf <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> and negligible internal resistance. The deflections produced in the tangent galvanometers A and B are <math><mn>30</mn><mo>°</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>60</mn><mo>°</mo></math> respectively. If A has&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> turns, then the number of turns <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> must have is",
    "image": null
